config FREETZ_LIB_libopenzwave
	bool "libopenzwave (libopenzwave.so)"
	default n
	select FREETZ_LIB_libstdcxx
	help
		OpenZWave is a C++ library that provides an interface to the
		Z-Wave home automation protocol. It talks to the controller
		stick through a plain serial device (/dev/ttyUSB*,
		/dev/ttyACM*), so it does not need libusb; the bundled hidapi
		back end (and with it libudev) stays disabled on this target.
		The Z-Wave device database lives in Domoticz's own Config
		directory, which is why it is not installed twice. The Domoticz
		package points its build at this library explicitly, because its
		own detection would not find the headers in
		usr/include/openzwave.

		This is the master branch of OpenZWave, not the v1.6 release:
		Domoticz includes ValueIDIndexesDefines.h, a header that the
		release predates. The commit is pinned, the build is the same as
		the release one (same soname, same install layout).
